1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
This video introduces 2D function related updates for everyone.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
In the 2025.0 version, we launched the AI version of the generator, which is used to make paper samples.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Now it is further enhanced on this basis, and can support the input of real images.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Select the main menu bar 2D.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Open the version generator.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Select the clothing type according to the measurement value of the generated parameterized version.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
In addition, you can also use the AI version of the generator.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It is located in the upper right corner of the generator.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Click to open a new window.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Here you can choose to enter a hint to describe the clothing you want or upload a reference picture.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
From the 2025.1 version, you can choose to upload real images.

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Click to switch to image options.

13
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Click to upload the clothing you want.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
After uploading, click to start generation.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
CLO will automatically draw the paper sample according to the photos uploaded.

16
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
You can preview it in the window of the 2D version.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
As long as the generation is completed, click to close.

18
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
You can also continue to modify the measurement value in the version generator to get close to the ideal effect.

19
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Finally, click to create.

20
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
The paper sample will be placed in the 2D window.

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Now, the simple image will be converted into a custom version of the online store image you like.

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
It becomes more intuitive and convenient.

23
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Make the design more relaxed.

24
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
In the 2025.1 version, you can be more flexible.

25
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Define the time limit and the time limit as the number point or non-number point.

26
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
The number point follows the set number rule.

27
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
The non-number point will smartly adapt to the movement of the number point.

28
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
To maintain the exact proportion of the whole paper.

29
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Use the edit number tool to select the actual point on the sheet.

30
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
To make it easier to identify.

31
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Now the number point edge will be displayed in green.

32
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Right-click on one of the number points.

33
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You can convert it to a non-number point.

34
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The non-number point will return to the standard appearance without green highlights.

35
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
You can also select the frame or press the Shift key.

36
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Choose multiple number points to convert.

37
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,000
The non-number point will change according to the number point movement.

38
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Of course, you can also convert the point back to the number point.

39
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:47,000
So that when adjusting other points, the number point rule of this point is fixed.

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Similarly, if you use the edit curve number tool.

41
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
You can also change the number point.

42
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Then you can identify the number point of the curve point.

43
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:06,000
You can convert the curve point to a number point or a non-number point.

44
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Through this update.

45
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Users can control the number point more accurately.

46
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
In the previous version.

47
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
The inner line on the symmetrical board cannot be directly aligned to the symmetrical axis.

48
